  <section class="section mist" id="paid">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="kicker">Why sell, and what you get</p>
        <h2>You are paid for records you already have.</h2>
        <p>Nothing is built, bought or shipped. The buyer licenses a copy of records your company made in the ordinary course of work, and pays your company for it. The program we introduce companies to publishes <strong>$100K&ndash;$5M</strong> for an operating archive, and that band is a ceiling rather than a forecast.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="checks reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-doc"/></svg></span>
          <h3>The buyer pays you, not us</h3>
          <p>The license is between your company and the data buyer. We are paid by the buyer for the introduction, so nothing is taken out of what your company receives.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-doccheck"/></svg></span>
          <h3>You see the number before you sign</h3>
          <p>Scope, term and price are set in the agreement in writing. Nothing is delivered, and nothing is charged, until you approve it.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-clock"/></svg></span>
          <h3>About three months to payment</h3>
          <p>Paid about 60 days after signature, following 15&ndash;30 days of processing, on the buyer&rsquo;s published terms.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal"><strong>Who signs what:</strong> we make the introduction and stay in the deal as the go-between, but the license is signed between your company and the data buyer. We are not the buyer, and not a party to that agreement.</p>
      <p class="muted small-note reveal">What a dataset is worth depends on the records, the rights and the terms, so we do not put a price on yours before reviewing it. <a href="market.html">What AI data sells for</a> collects the figures buyers publish themselves, so you can see the range before you talk to anyone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

