        <h2>Four questions, about a minute.</h2>
        <p>These are the published minimums of the buyer program we introduce companies to, and the four questions below follow them. Your company also has to own the records in those systems. If the answer is no, we say so on this page rather than on a call. Nothing you enter here is stored &mdash; see our <a href="privacy.html">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fit-panel reveal">
        <div class="fit-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span id="fit-bar"></span></div>
        <p class="fit-count" id="fit-count">0 of 4 answered</p>
        <form class="qualifier" id="qualifier" novalidate>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>1. Does your company have at least 30 full-time staff &mdash; 10 or more for an accounting, finance or medical firm, 6 or more for a law firm?</legend>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="yes" required> Yes</label>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="no"> No</label>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>2. Has your company operated for at least 3 years, with those years of records still in your systems?</legend>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="yes"> Yes</label>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="no"> No</label>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>3. Does your business run on at least five systems &mdash; for example email, chat, file storage, CRM and a support or project tool?</legend>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="yes"> Yes</label>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="no"> No</label>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>4. Is at least half of your staff in the U.S., Canada, the U.K. or Australia?</legend>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="yes"> Yes</label>
            <label class="q-option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="no"> No</label>
          </fieldset>
          <p><button class="btn" type="submit">See my result</button></p>
        </form>
        <div class="q-result" id="q-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

