  <section class="section mist record-band" id="buyer-view">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-num">03</span>What a buyer sees</p>
        <h2>From your records to a licensed dataset.</h2>
        <p>A plain picture of the steps between your systems and a buyer. Nothing is shared until the rights are clear and you approve the terms.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">01</span>
          <h3>Your records</h3>
          <p>Customer threads, tickets, documents and deal notes as your team already keeps them.</p>
          <div class="sample-record"><b>Ticket 4821</b> &middot; Customer: [redacted]<br>Issue: billing sync failed<br>Resolution: re-authorized card<br>Handoff: [redacted] &middot; 14 Mar</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">02</span>
          <h3>Rights and PII review</h3>
          <p>The data buyer reviews contracts, customer terms and personal information before anything is shared.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">03</span>
          <h3>Scoped and de-identified</h3>
          <p>The data buyer removes or transforms personal identifiers, then reviews the copy again. Removing names alone does not make data anonymous.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step reveal">
          <span class="flow-num">04</span>
          <h3>Buyer sees the licensed scope</h3>
          <p>Scope, purpose and length of license are set in the terms you approve, and every introduction runs past you first.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="redact redact-demo" data-redact>
        <div class="redact-panel">
          <h3>In your systems</h3>
          <p class="redact-hint">Untick anything you would hold back.</p>
          <label class="redact-row redact-pick"><span><input type="checkbox" checked data-share="name"> Customer name</span><b>Avery Doe</b></label>
          <label class="redact-row redact-pick"><span><input type="checkbox" checked data-share="email"> Email address</span><b>avery@example.com</b></label>
          <label class="redact-row redact-pick"><span><input type="checkbox" checked data-share="account"> Account number</span><b>AC-4821-90</b></label>
          <label class="redact-row redact-pick"><span><input type="checkbox" checked data-share="issue"> Issue</span><b>billing sync failed</b></label>
          <label class="redact-row redact-pick"><span><input type="checkbox" checked data-share="resolution"> Resolution</span><b>card re-authorized</b></label>
        </div>
        <div class="redact-panel buyer">
          <h3>In the licensed scope</h3>
          <p class="redact-row" data-out="name"><span>Customer name</span><b data-show="[redacted]">[redacted]</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row" data-out="email"><span>Email address</span><b data-show="[redacted]">[redacted]</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row" data-out="account"><span>Account number</span><b data-show="[redacted]">[redacted]</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row" data-out="issue"><span>Issue</span><b data-show="billing sync failed">billing sync failed</b></p>
          <p class="redact-row" data-out="resolution"><span>Resolution</span><b data-show="card re-authorized">card re-authorized</b></p>
          <p class="redact-count"><b data-redact-count>5</b> of 5 fields in scope</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="scope reveal">
        <div class="scope-col">
          <h3>What usually can be licensed</h3>
          <ul class="scope-list">
            <li>Resolved tickets with the fix attached</li>
            <li>Playbooks, SOPs and their revision history</li>
            <li>Proposal and document history</li>
            <li>Deal notes, including why deals were lost</li>
            <li>Transcripts of business meetings and calls</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="scope-col off">
          <h3>What we will not take</h3>
          <ul class="scope-list">
            <li>Open litigation files, or anything under a protective order</li>
            <li>Records you cannot show a right to license</li>
            <li>Passwords, credentials and full card numbers</li>
            <li>Client files where the client has not agreed</li>
            <li>Health information without a documented consent path</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="flow-note">If what you hold is not on either list, ask. The answer usually arrives on the first call.</p>
      <p class="flow-note" data-redact-note>Illustrative example, not a real record. What you hold back is your call: a narrower scope is a smaller dataset, and the buyer prices what it can use. Every dataset is reviewed on its own terms. <a href="trust.html">How we handle your data</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

