  <section class="section ink" id="process">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-num">05</span>The process</p>
        <h2>From a first call to payment.</h2>
        <p>The order is fixed. The dates are not, and pretending otherwise would waste your time.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="timeline">
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="timeline-num">01</span>
          <h3>A short call</h3>
          <p>What you hold, which systems, and whether it clears the published floors.</p>
          <span class="slows">Half an hour, and you can stop there.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="timeline-num">02</span>
          <h3>Scope outline</h3>
          <p>We map the categories worth reviewing and flag what looks unlicensable early.</p>
          <span class="slows">Slowed by contracts that say nothing about third-party use.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="timeline-num">03</span>
          <h3>Buyer diligence</h3>
          <p>Each interested buyer checks rights and personal data in its own process.</p>
          <span class="slows">Slowed by records nobody can export cleanly.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="timeline-num">04</span>
          <h3>The lab reviews</h3>
          <p>The buyer takes the agreed scope to the AI lab that would use it.</p>
          <span class="slows">Slowed by a lab shifting its data priorities.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <span class="timeline-num">05</span>
          <h3>Payment</h3>
          <p>Paid about 60 days after signature, following 15&ndash;30 days of processing, on the buyer&rsquo;s published terms.</p>
          <span class="slows">Slowed by an incomplete delivery manifest.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="timeline-note reveal">About three months from the first conversation to payment is the buyer&rsquo;s own expectation. The clock sits in stages three to five, not with us. You approve the scope before anything is delivered, and you can stop at any stage.</p>
      <p class="link-row reveal"><a href="how-it-works.html">How it works in detail</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

